@alexey-ivanov-es 
>As I understand - no. The first step in data stream migration is to do a rollover, which creates a new write index for the data stream and all write requests will be send to it. And this new index was created with the current version, so doesn't need migration. 

That is correct: if the write index needs to be upgraded, we first do a rollover, so that the new write index has version 8.x .  Most writes should then go to the new write index, but it is still possible that writes go to the other backing indices if the backing indices are written too directly (rather than through the data stream name). Because of this, we actually do set a read-only block on the source backing indices while doing the reindex.

